WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.510
LARRY ARNN: You're saying that
these people are not angels.

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:07.440
If they get a discretion,
sooner or later some of them

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.778
are going to abuse it.

00:00:08.778 --> 00:00:10.770
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:19.710
In our Constitution reader,
we read the Progressives.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:25.110
John Dewey's argument is, it's
a new world, really different.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:29.610
And as the world changes,
he goes on to argue,

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.400
it changes how we think.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.200
John Dewey says,
those principles

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.730
in the Declaration
of Independence,

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:39.570
he says those fit for a
pioneer-agrarian society.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:43.410
People thought like
that, right, back then.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.950
And so everything's changed now.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:48.620
The old idea was, we're human.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.410
We're capable of really great
things, says the Federalist.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:56.000
And we're capable of really bad
things, says the Federalist.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.940
And so we need to arrange the
government so that there's

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.490
a bias in favor of the
good things we can do.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:04.760
And government should be
limited, just strong enough

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:07.850
to protect us from one another.

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:11.540
And don't give it absolute
power, because men are not

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:13.970
angels, true enough, and
they have to have government,

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:15.950
but angels do not govern men.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.390
That's one world.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:21.500
And another world is, wow,
look how much more we can

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.170
do by using these techniques.

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:25.340
Let's do it.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:26.300
Let's get going here.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:26.800
Right?

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.380
Let's solve these problems.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:32.540
Let's get these checks and
balances out of the way.

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.710
Let's stop this
kind of government

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:37.370
that's offset against
itself so it's always

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:40.610
hampered and always a problem.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:41.330
Right?

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.130
That's the argument.

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:46.190
And if you just look at the
power of modern science,

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:49.010
look at the incredible
things it can achieve,

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:52.670
doesn't that argument
have great force?

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:53.570
But you tell me.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.430
What's wrong with the argument?

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:55.970
SPEAKER 1: I don't
know that I'll

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:57.595
be able to fully
developed this, but it

00:01:57.595 --> 00:01:59.880
seems like the last
couple of days,

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.840
we've really established
that the true genius

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:06.740
of the Constitution was
separating the sovereignty

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.590
from the power and keeping
those two things separate so

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:12.590
that they can check one another
and keep an eye on one another.

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:15.500
It seems as you move towards
this bureaucratic structure

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.640
that we're talking about,
you create other tyrants.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:23.180
You create health problems or
economic problems as tyrants.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:25.460
So in order to combat
that, you have to--

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:28.820
they're arguing to recombine
that sovereignty and the power

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:31.560
and put them in the same
hands to combat that.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.370
But then we forget that
fundamental principle

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:36.020
in the Declaration
of Independence,

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:37.490
"all men are created equal."

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:40.910
And when we yoke the
sovereignty and power again,

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:43.370
then we challenge
that very thing

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:45.510
that all men are created equal.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.330
LARRY ARNN: You mean--

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:48.120
you're nodding.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.203
What are you going to say?

00:02:49.203 --> 00:02:51.560
SPEAKER 2: Well, we're talking
about how whether or not

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.390
the principles of
the Constitution

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:56.460
still apply in a
radically different world.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.030
But even if it were
not an agrarian society

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:03.350
anymore, we're still
a society of humans,

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:06.680
and human nature doesn't change.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.170
We still suffer
from the same ills

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:11.383
and make the same mistakes.

00:03:11.383 --> 00:03:13.550
LARRY ARNN: So you're both
saying in different ways,

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.380
your argument is like
Madison's argument.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:19.762
You're saying that these
people are not angels.

00:03:19.762 --> 00:03:20.470
SPEAKER 1: Right.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:21.220
LARRY ARNN: Right?

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:28.680
And so if they get a discretion,
sooner or later some of them

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.060
are going to abuse it.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.980
You're saying that
doesn't change.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:36.600
And you're saying that's nature.

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:39.660
The excellence of the
human being is nature.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:43.080
And the fallings of the
human being are nature.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.330
And nature doesn't
change, because remember,

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:47.880
we defined this term, nature.

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:48.900
Right?

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:51.820
And this term, nature,
governs, it starts with babies,

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.610
it starts with seeds.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.620
But then it includes
this fallenness

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:59.220
of human beings, right,
this capable of greatness,

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:03.700
capable of evil, both, and
that arrangement of government.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.730
And if you set out
to overcome that,

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.890
then here's the final question.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:14.880
If you can design your
society any way you want to,

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:21.070
what standard will
you use to design it?

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.740
What can give you any guidance?

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:25.810
I can tell you what
happened in Nazi Germany,

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:28.990
right, because they just
go right down this road.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:31.660
And what it means
is the guide that

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:34.960
remains after everything
else has been eliminated

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.820
is strength.

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:38.980
Only power can arbitrate.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:42.610
Now, what that
means, then, I argue,

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:46.090
is that these problems that
come up in society, sure enough,

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:48.370
one of the reasons we
have the government

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:51.050
is to help solve these problems.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:53.440
But if we think about
it, we understand

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.750
that, yeah, of course, we
need to make things better

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:56.530
in society.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:59.180
We need to treat people as
well as we can treat them.

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:01.660
But also we have to
be a little suspicious

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:04.450
of concentrating power.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:05.870
SPEAKER 3: Thank
you for watching.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:07.870
We hope you're enjoying
our Highlights series

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.750
and invite you to explore
all of Hillsdale College's

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:11.950
online courses.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:16.110
They are free and for
everyone who loves to learn.

